  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the resignation of Gibran Rakabuming Raka from the vice presidency, President Prabowo Subianto is set to propose two potential successors to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) of the Republic of Indonesia. Representatives from the MPR have confirmed receipt of information regarding the President’s scheduled visit to the legislative complex in Senayan, Jakarta, to formally submit these names. This process, which involves deliberations among political coalition leaders, is intended to fill the vacant position. Discussions regarding potential candidates have included various political figures and party members, with ongoing preparations by the MPR’s verification teams to oversee the selection and appointment procedures. The move marks a significant transition in the current administration as the legislative branch prepares for a joint session to address the vice presidential vacancy.",
